Z||000004||Feenx||02-22-2001||02:33 AM||||if you take a close look at the speedo in the pic......it looks like a 85mph.<BR>I think that there just White face stickers with blue lights.<BR>I have white face gauges on my 86 coupe and I tried the blue bulb trick and got the same effect....looks great but hard on the eyes while driving...but I love the Fiero Logo in the center though..<BR>my white face stickers cost me $15. at  <BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm</A> <BR>------------------<BR>86 Sport Coupe (Red)<BR>2.5L Auto<P>[This message has been edited by Feenx (edited 02-22-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Feenx (edited 02-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||CozmoPooky||02-22-2001||09:16 AM||||I've been contemplating this idea for quite a while...<BR>I think they're using a Panasonic EL element for a light source <A HREF="http://info.digikey.com/T011/v4/661.pdf" TARGET=_blank>http://info.digikey.com/T011/v4/661.pdf</A>  which is a sheet about 4" x 6" you can cut to fit. It is available in blue (shown), green, white, yellow/orange, yellow/green and red. The light output is rated in "candles per square meter" (phew!) with the yellow/green the brightest (65 cd/m2) and red the dimmest (15 cd/m2). I'm not sure how this relates to what we need, and I don't know if you can dim them. You also need the power inverter to drive it and backlit gauges. To do all the gauges (GT included) 2 sheets and 2 inverters would be required as well as some way to drop the input voltage to the inverters to 5 volts. This would not be cheap, as the sheets are $37 ea. and the inverters are $12 ea. I agree, orief, the blue would drive most people batty after a while but with a different color choice and some "finessing" they could be very cool looking. I'm going to get some to play with anyway, but for $80 on Ebay that's CHEEP if he's using the parts I think he is. (white face gauges included!)<P>------------------<BR>Cozmo<BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>'87 Duke Coupe     <BR>'85 2M6 Targa<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bothfierossig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
